# PAEOS Reasoning Continuity Layer (RCL) System Design
## Version 0.1

This document outlines the system design (component graph, interfaces, data flow, and state machines) for implementing the Reasoning Continuity Layer (RCL) as proposed in the RB v0.1 specification.

---

## 1. Component Graph

The system is organized into the following logical components:

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph RCL[Reasoning Continuity Layer]
        subgraph state[State Management]
            Store[State Store]
            Version[Versioning Engine]
            Reconcile[Reconciliation Engine]
        end
        
        subgraph models[Domain Models]
            Mission[Mission]
            Decision[Decision]
            Evidence[Evidence]
            Checkpoint[Checkpoint]
            Package[Context Package]
        end
        
        subgraph extraction[State Extraction & Update]
            Classifier[Statement Classifier]
            Updater[State Updater]
            Provenance[Provenance Tracker]
        end
        
        subgraph context[Context Construction]
            Builder[Context Builder]
            Policy[Context Policies]
            Ranker[Relevance Ranker]
            Compressor[Compressor]
        end
        
        subgraph handoff[Handoff & Persistence]
            Export[State Exporter]
            Import[State Importer]
            Checkpointer[Checkpoint Manager]
        end
        
        subgraph providers[Provider Layer]
            Interface[Provider Neutral Interface]
            Adapters[Provider Adapters]
        end
    end

    state --> models
    extraction --> state
    context --> state
    context --> models
    handoff --> state
    providers --> context
```

